      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to the [[credential-scoping]] page, the Anthropic API key is **injected into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts**. \n\nThe key specifics are:\n\n- A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n- The key is injected **only into the child process environment** \u2014 not into the Hub\u0027s own process environment\n- This means the Hub process itself never holds the credential in its environment variables\n- The same scoping model applies to the Query agent: it also receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time, never inherited from the Hub\n\nThis architecture prevents a compromised or misbehaving Hub process from leaking the credential simply by inspecting its own environment variables.",
